Z||000042||Slammed Fiero||06-21-2001||01:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTBro:<BR><B>Unlike some of you guys.  I have good luck with girls and my Fiero.  My ex-girlfriend loved my car.  She mostly just liked going fast.<P>But I guess my Fiero wasn't fast enough for her because she dumped me...<P>Now I am a single guy with a Fiero.  I have to fight the girls off!!!  <P>No!!! Really!!!  <BR>They never pay attention to me!!  <P>Only my car!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah my Ex Girlfriend Kinda liked my Fiero. The only thing she didn't like is that is was faster than hers (haha)<P>I have had the pleasure of having women look at my car , yell stuff, it's a real ego booster. Until they see me (haha) I don't think they realize it's a pontiac.<P>Then again , I was downtown one night and 2 chicks in a Hundyai (sp?) pull up next to me , they rev the motor (cool chicks ) She yells to me .."Your not going to win it's a new tiburon" <P>Ohhhhhhhh TAY<BR>I beat them like a rented mule ..next light ..<P>"nice Car!!"<P>haha . i asked them if they were even trying ...they took offense , because they were!<P>go 2.8 go! <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals. &lt;b&gt; New White Face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS&lt;/b&gt;Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000043||Tweek||06-21-2001||01:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero2:<BR><B>I love my Fiero. I hope to have a better sig pic too as soon as my husband Steve (Fiero5) get's it changed.<BR>I don't like them with the hoods and stuff up.<BR> <BR>Welcome.<P>Marian<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Marion, Im curious...   How did you car start out life? as in year + model. I like it though. Formula decals.. Duke.. (I have one, so thats not a flame) and fastback. Im my opinion its ok for cars to have identity crisis', as long as they stay the same model.. like 100% Fiero. Yesterday I saw a Type R Cavalier..   I was LMAO at him...||||reg||1
